WEBVTT

NOTE Timing is estimated from script and acoustic pauses; listening review pending.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.297
It is now 10:24 a.m. Valentina
has moved from a long

00:00:10.297 --> 00:00:14.535
investigation summary to
a clear decision request.

00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:18.470
She has not hidden uncertainty, invented
inventory, or promised delivery.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:23.538
She has separated confirmed facts
from assumptions, recommended a

00:00:23.538 --> 00:00:28.340
practical direction, and named
the handoffs that follow approval.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:33.065
Before she sends, she performs
the seven-point check.

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:38.395
Is the decision clear? Does the
first sentence state the conclusion?

00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:43.675
Is every fact necessary? Is the
impact quantified where possible?

00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:45.930
Is there a recommendation?

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.165
Are owner and timing clear?

00:00:48.165 --> 00:00:50.845
Does the detail fit this audience?

00:00:50.845 --> 00:00:53.125
The message is not valuable
because it sounds executive.

00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:58.453
It is valuable because it
makes responsible action

00:00:58.453 --> 00:01:02.425
easier. Accurate information
establishes credibility.

00:01:02.425 --> 00:01:05.730
Decision-ready
communication creates value.
